 "_doc": "Display literals in layout scripts (text/layout_refs.json 'literals'). Each is added as a new key of 'table' so the layout's literal resolves to Korean. Literals not listed stay as-is: internal element names (CharName, InputName, PlayerName, mode, profile_message, xbox*, BUTTON*/PROMPT*, cursor/join/charname labels), the NTSC/PAL test and video-mode screens (arial14, not reached on NTSC USA), and dev text 'Title!!!'. Wave/duel names (Barfight_Wave3_*, Bridge_Lost_SecondWave_*, Tomb_Duel_*) are element names whose text is set at runtime. 'Chapter N' book headings are literals: the SWAT-only lvl_frontend table holding such keys is not loaded. Also not translated: numbers, 'P-1'..'P-4'/'CPU'/'N/A' (woodcut_small poster tags), 'Xbox Live', 'LITERAL'. Code-referenced literals (text/code_literals.json) are translated here too.",
